From 943072aedcafc5de38af7d789041fb83164a9128 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Luca Casati <luk00casati@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 08:15:05 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 5/6] bwn: N-PHY: wait for the first 2057 RC calibration run

RCCAL_DONE_OSCCAP still shows the previous run's done bit for a few us
after a start, and the first (SCAP) run polled it immediately, so the
run was stopped before it happened. RCCAL_SCAP_VAL then read 0 (wl
gets 8 on a BCM43228), which detunes the TX low-pass filter set up in
the rev7+ workarounds. Wait before polling, as the other two runs do.

Port of the Linux b43 fix "b43: N-PHY: wait for the first 2057 RC
calibration run".

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 sys/gnu/dev/bwn/phy_n/if_bwn_phy_n_core.c | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/sys/gnu/dev/bwn/phy_n/if_bwn_phy_n_core.c b/sys/gnu/dev/bwn/phy_n/if_bwn_phy_n_core.c
index d739200..3b8ad3a 100644
--- a/sys/gnu/dev/bwn/phy_n/if_bwn_phy_n_core.c
+++ b/sys/gnu/dev/bwn/phy_n/if_bwn_phy_n_core.c
@@ -1029,6 +1029,7 @@ static uint16_t bwn_radio_2057_rccal(struct bwn_mac *mac)
 
 	/* Start, wait, stop */
 	BWN_RF_WRITE(mac, R2057_RCCAL_START_R1_Q1_P1, 0x55);
+	DELAY(140);
 	if (!bwn_radio_wait_value(mac, R2057_RCCAL_DONE_OSCCAP, 2, 2, 500,
 				  5000000))
 		BWN_DBGPRINTF(mac, "Radio 0x2057 rccal timeout\n");
